==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsuːpa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːpa|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
First attested in the 17th century. Probably at least partially a loanword from {{etyl|gml|is}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|súpu|súpur}}

# [[soup]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|s|ú|p|n=?}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[borga alla súpuna]]
* [[kjötsúpa]] (clear soup containing meat)
* [[súpukjöt]] (meat, especially [[mutton]] for making soup)
* [[súpuskál]] ((soup) [[tureen]])
* [[súputeningur]] ([[soup cube]], [[bouillon cube]])
* [[uxahalasúpa]] ([[oxtail soup]])

=====See also=====
* [[soð]]
* [[vellingur]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|súpa|lang=non}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|sūpanan|lang=is}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|saup|supu|sopið}}

# to [[sip]], [[drink]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-s2|s|ú|p|mp=-}}

=====Derived terms=====
